<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Reddi Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1325 CE – 1448 CE (approx.) · capital Kondavidu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Telugu kingdom of coastal Andhra founded after the fall of the Kakatiyas, known for its forts and its literary court.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prolaya-vema-reddi">Prolaya Vema Reddi</a>, a former Kakatiya follower, joined the revolt of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/musunuri-nayaks">Musunuri Nayaks</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and around 1325 established his own rule in coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-region">Andhra</a>. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addanki">Addanki</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondavidu">Kondavidu</a> his capital, and the dynasty extended along the coast from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna-river">Krishna</a> to the Godavari.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Reddi kings ruled through a network of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondavidu">Kondavidu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondapalli">Kondapalli</a> and controlled the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/motupalli">Motupalli</a>, encouraging trade. Their court supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telugu-language">Telugu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> literature: the great poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srinatha">Srinatha</a> served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedakomati-vema-reddi">Pedakomati Vema</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/errana">Errana</a> completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-mahabharatam">Telugu Mahabharata</a>. The kings granted land generously to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> and temples.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Caught between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gajapati-kingdom">Gajapatis of Odisha</a>, the Reddis lost territory steadily. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondavidu">Kondavidu</a> fell to Vijayanagara around 1424, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajahmundry">Rajahmundry</a> branch was absorbed by the Gajapati Kingdom by 1448.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/reddi-kingdom.jpg" alt="Reddi Kingdom" width="320" height="356"><figcaption>Image: Pedhireddi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reddi_KIngdom_at_its_peakl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1325 CE – 1448 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kondavidu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Prolaya Vema Reddi, Pedakomati Vema</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Telugu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Reddi dynasty, Reddis of Kondavidu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1386&amp;focus=reddi-kingdom" aria-label="Reddi Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6861 1590 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Reddi Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7181 1846L7018 1385M7181 1846L7310 1674"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1385h0M7310 1674h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7181 1846h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7181 1846h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1386&amp;focus=reddi-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
